<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spanish reconquest of Santo Domingo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1808–1809</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Spanish reconquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> was the campaign of 1808–1809 in which Dominican <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">creoles</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-sanchez-ramirez">Juan Sánchez Ramírez</a>, with British naval help, drove the French from the eastern part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a>, ceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1795. After victory at Palo Hincado in November 1808 they besieged the city of Santo Domingo, which surrendered in July 1809, and the colony returned to Spanish rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spanish-reconquest-of-santo-domingo.jpg" alt="Spanish reconquest of Santo Domingo" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Risantana · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hispaniola_history_map_18stage.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
